# Template for the .env this repository reads. Copy it and fill in the values:
#
#     cp env.default .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way — it holds the Google Sheet IDs,
# which ARE the credentials. Both sheets are shared as "anyone with the link"
# because the CSV export we fetch is unauthenticated, so knowing a sheet's ID is
# knowing enough to read it. That is also why they are not in the code, not in
# the Git history, and never on the published dashboard.
#
# In GitHub Actions these are repository secrets of the same names, set with
# `gh secret set BABEL_VALIDATION_SHEET_ID` (and likewise for the blocklist).
#
# Anything unset here simply turns off the tests that need it — see each entry.
# Nothing below is needed for `pytest -m unit`, which is entirely offline.
#
# NOTE FOR CODING AGENTS: fill this in by writing to .env, and do not read .env
# back or echo it. See CLAUDE.md, "Untrusted Input".


# The Babel Validation Google Sheet: ~2000 test cases pulled at collection time
# by tests/nodenorm/test_nodenorm_from_gsheet.py and the NameRes equivalent.
# Without it those tests fail at collection with "No Google Sheet ID".
#
# The ID is the long path segment of the sheet's URL, between /d/ and /edit:
#
#     https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/THIS_PART_HERE/edit#gid=0
#
# Twenty or more characters of [A-Za-z0-9_-], no quotes and no spaces around the
# `=`; resolve_sheet_id() rejects anything else, which is mostly there to catch
# a quoted value pasted in from a shell. Ask a maintainer for the ID.
BABEL_VALIDATION_SHEET_ID=

# The blocklist sheet, read by tests/nameres/test_blocklist.py. Same format, a
# different sheet, and a different secret — do not reuse the ID above.
#
# This one is the more sensitive of the two: the dashboard withholds blocklist
# test detail entirely because the sheet may not be public, so never add it to a
# test ID, a report field or a link.
BABEL_VALIDATION_BLOCKLIST_SHEET_ID=

# A GitHub token for tests/github_issues/, which reads BabelTest assertions out
# of issue bodies across the repositories listed in tests/targets.ini.
#
# Public repositories only, so a classic token with NO scopes ticked is enough
# (or a fine-grained token with read-only access to public repositories). It is
# used for the higher rate limit, not for access.
#
# Without it those tests skip — which is a green run that tested nothing, so if
# you are working on them, check the run summary says they ran. To deliberately
# test the no-token path, set this to empty rather than deleting the line:
# dotenv does not override a variable already present in the environment.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional. Where the Google Sheet CSV and GitHub issue caches are written;
# defaults to a 0700 directory under your home. Set it to keep them somewhere
# else — never to a shared location such as /tmp, since the issue cache decides
# what a later run fetches and executes.
# BABEL_VALIDATION_CACHE_DIR=
